rry powder","qty":""},{"item":"2 tbsp","qty":""},{"item":"12.6 g","qty":""},{"item":"n/a","qty":""},{"item":"Water","qty":""},{"item":"1 ¼ cups","qty":""},{"item":"296.25 g","qty":""},{"item":"n/a","qty":""},{"item":"Cumin powder","qty":""},{"item":"1 pinch","qty":""},{"item":"0.14 g","qty":""},{"item":"n/a","qty":""},{"item":"Salt","qty":""},{"item":"1 tsp","qty":""},{"item":"6 g","qty":""},{"item":"n/a","qty":""},{"item":"Pepper","qty":""},{"item":"colspan=\"5\" style=\"text-align: center; background: #f5f5f5;;\" |Other","qty":""},{"item":"Oil for frying","qty":""},{"item":"1 cup","qty":""},{"item":"218 g","qty":""},{"item":"n/a","qty":""},{"item":"Hot pepper to taste","qty":""},{"item":"Mango chutney to taste","qty":""}],"steps":["In large bowl combine flour, salt, turmeric, cumin, sugar and yeast.","Add enough lukewarm water to make a soft dough. Mix well, cover and let rise 2 hours.","Boil soaked chickpeas in salted water until tender. Drain well.","Heat oil in a heavy skillet, add garlic, onion, and curry powder mixed with ¼ cup (60 ml) water; sauté for a few minutes.","Add chickpeas, stir to coat well and cook for 5 minutes. Add 1 cup water, cumin, salt and pepper.","Cover, lower heat and simmer until peas are soft; add more water if necessary. When chickpeas are finished they should be soft and moist; adjust seasoning.","Punch down dough and allow to relax for 15 minutes.","To shape bara, take about 1 tablespoon of dough, pat with both hands to flatten to a circle 4–5 inches in diameter; use water to moisten palms of hands.","Fry a few baras at a time in hot oil; turn once and drain on kitchen paper.","Make a sandwich by placing 2 tablespoons of cooked chickpeas between 2 baras.","Add pepper sauce and mango chutney to taste."],"tags":[],"youtube":"","culture":null,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}